/P 151 0 R
/T (Using manual open\(\)/close\(\) inside try/finally can be made correct if every file handle is closed in the finally block. A with statement is shorter andmanages closure automatically. Both approaches have O\(n\) time for n characters/records and O\(1\) extra working memory when streaming. Neither changes asymptotic complexity. With a single log file, a failure duringwriting can leave one handle open in a poorly structured manual version; with properly nested with statements, each entered context manager closes its file during stack unwinding. The number of open filesis bounded by the number of simultaneously nested with blocks. )
/E (Using manual open\(\)/close\(\) inside try/finally can be made correct if every file handle is closed in the finally block. A with statement is shorter andmanages closure automatically. Both approaches have O\(n\) time for n characters/records and O\(1\) extra working memory when streaming. Neither changes asymptotic complexity. With a single log file, a failure duringwriting can leave one handle open in a poorly structured manual version; with properly nested with statements, each entered context manager closes its file during stack unwinding. The number of open filesis bounded by the number of simultaneously nested with blocks. )
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
