505 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 155 0 R
/T (Keeping every function in one script avoids package import setup and has no separate package-loading step. A package adds a one-time import/loading cost for each module in a fresh process; Python caches imported modules in sys.modules, so later imports in the same process normally reuse them. Import time depends on module size and dependencies and is not a per-record processing cost. A package uses some extra memory for module objects and their globals, but this is generally small compared with the attendance data. Finding and changing a function is easiest in the package because each responsibility has a predictable file; in a single script, a developer must search one larger file and be careful not to disturb unrelated code. The data-processing )
/E (Keeping every function in one script avoids package import setup and has no separate package-loading step. A package adds a one-time import/loading cost for each module in a fresh process; Python caches imported modules in sys.modules, so later imports in the same process normally reuse them. Import time depends on module size and dependencies and is not a per-record processing cost. A package uses some extra memory for module objects and their globals, but this is generally small compared with the attendance data. Finding and changing a function is easiest in the package because each responsibility has a predictable file; in a single script, a developer must search one larger file and be careful not to disturb unrelated code. The data-processing )
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [44]
>>
endobj
