1378 0 obj
<<
/Title (Using manual open\(\)/close\(\) inside try/finally can be made correct if every file handle is closed in the finally block. A with statement is shorter andmanages closure automatically. Both approaches have O\(n\) time for n characters/records and O\(1\) extra working memory when streaming. Neither changes asymptotic complexity. With a single log file, a failure duringwriting can leave one handle open in a poorly structured manual version; with properly nested with statements, each entered context manager closes its file during stack unwinding. The number of open filesis bounded by the number of simultaneously nested with blocks.)
/Dest [20 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1376 0 R
>>
endobj
